InpUseCleanedLabels
only controls whether
is_flagged
is actually used to filter the training rows. That's a deliberate design choice: the printed audit stats (n_total, n_flagged, est_noise_rate) are always available for logging, even on a raw-label run, without changing what that run actually trades on. It also means a raw-labels run and a cleaned-labels run at the same
InpPruneAggressiveness
always report identical audit numbers in the Journal - which is exactly what I saw across my own runs, and a useful sanity check that the branch is wired correctly rather than silently changing what gets audited.
The other input that matters here is
InpMinTrainSamples
. If a given refit window doesn't produce at least this many candidates, the whole refit is skipped for that cycle rather than forcing a fit on too little data - the same "refuse rather than fit badly" philosophy as the guard inside
CLogRegClassifier::Train
from the previous section.
The EA: Risk and Order Management
This section is not specific to confident learning - it's the standing order-management discipline I apply to every EA I publish. It matters here because changes in approval rate change how often the order-management path is exercised. The aggressiveness-1.0 run approved 71 trades against the raw run's 24, and every one of those extra 47 trades still had to pass through the same margin, minimum-lot, and stop-distance guards below - a sizing bug that only shows up rarely would have been three times more likely to surface in that run purely from trade-count exposure. The guards below must stay identical across runs to keep the comparison valid. Four guards, in order: clamp by real margin (not just the risk formula), never round a sub-minimum lot up, floor the stop distance by the broker's real minimum before sizing, and clamp to both the per-order limit and the symbol maximum.
ComputeRiskNormalizedLots
//+------------------------------------------------------------------+
//| ComputeRiskNormalizedLots                                        |
//+------------------------------------------------------------------+
double
ComputeRiskNormalizedLots
(
const
double
sl_distance_price,
const
bool
is_buy)
  {
double
tick_value = SymbolInfoDouble(_Symbol,SYMBOL_TRADE_TICK_VALUE);
double
tick_size  = SymbolInfoDouble(_Symbol,SYMBOL_TRADE_TICK_SIZE);
if
(tick_size <= 0.0 || tick_value <= 0.0)
return
(0.0);
// symbol spec is unusable
double
loss_per_lot = (sl_distance_price / tick_size) * tick_value;
if
(loss_per_lot <= 0.0)
return
(0.0);
double
risk_amount = AccountInfoDouble(ACCOUNT_BALANCE) * InpRiskPercent / 100.0;
double
raw_lots     = risk_amount / loss_per_lot;
double
lot_step  = SymbolInfoDouble(_Symbol,SYMBOL_VOLUME_STEP);
double
lot_min   = SymbolInfoDouble(_Symbol,SYMBOL_VOLUME_MIN);
double
lot_max   = SymbolInfoDouble(_Symbol,SYMBOL_VOLUME_MAX);
double
lot_limit = SymbolInfoDouble(_Symbol,SYMBOL_VOLUME_LIMIT);
//--- rounded DOWN, never to nearest: rounding up would quietly risk
//--- more than InpRiskPercent
double
lots = (lot_step > 0.0 ? MathFloor(raw_lots / lot_step) * lot_step : raw_lots);
//--- rule (2): below the broker minimum, skip the trade rather than
//--- force it up to lot_min
if
(lots < lot_min)
return
(0.0);
//--- rule (4): clamp to BOTH the per-order limit and the max, not
//--- the max alone
if
(lot_limit > 0.0)
      lots = MathMin(lots,lot_limit);
if
(lot_max > 0.0)
      lots = MathMin(lots,lot_max);
//--- rule (1): re-clamp by actual free margin, not the risk formula's
//--- assumption that margin is always available
double
price = (is_buy ? SymbolInfoDouble(_Symbol,SYMBOL_ASK) : SymbolInfoDouble(_Symbol,SYMBOL_BID));
double
margin_required = 0.0;
   ENUM_ORDER_TYPE order_type = (is_buy ? ORDER_TYPE_BUY : ORDER_TYPE_SELL);
if
(OrderCalcMargin(order_type,_Symbol,lots,price,margin_required) && margin_required > 0.0)
     {
double
free_margin = AccountInfoDouble(ACCOUNT_MARGIN_FREE);
if
(margin_required > free_margin)
        {
double
scale = free_margin / margin_required;
         lots = (lot_step > 0.0 ? MathFloor((lots * scale) / lot_step) * lot_step : lots * scale);
        }
     }
if
(lots < lot_min)
return
(0.0);
// margin clamp pushed it back below minimum
return
(lots);
  }
